{
  "inShort": "Behind: the sprint shows a landscape photo and a film thumbnail, not a playable slice. The devlog reports five testers, but supplies neither a build nor playtest notes. What was implemented and tested remains unknown, leaving the checkpoint goal unverified.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474vj00k1k9z85tgw7gsa",
      "text": "The public repository matches the task: Godot demos, an MIT license and import instructions. It provides reference projects, not evidence of the game's playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474w200k2k9z8zz6mezdu",
      "text": "The art-style reference remains done. Inspection reached only the Big Buck Bunny title and thumbnail, so the animation could not be verified. The sprint links that same film, not footage of the game."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474wh00k3k9z823f1jo7o",
      "text": "The inspected Wikipedia article supplies the promised playtesting reference. It does not document the five reported players or what they learned."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474wy00k4k9z8bbq9qdph",
      "text": "The private design board remains done. Its contents were not supplied for this review."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvu474xb00k5k9z8pgq871bc",
      "text": "The trailer storyboard was cut. No downloadable slice was shown instead, and the landscape photo demonstrates neither islands nor tides. Mia's work has gone unconfirmed for two weeks, leaving programming capacity for the playable slice uncertain."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Is there a downloadable build showing two islands, the tide loop and two-player sailing, with launch instructions and controls?",
    "Where are the five players' notes showing whether they could sail together and understand the tide loop?"
  ]
}

